<sn><md>### Example {.text-center}

#### Initial State

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-md-6
**`main` Branch**

```text
App/
assets/
auth/
layout/
temp/

```
:::

:::.col-12 .col-md-6
**`ui` Branch**

```text
assets/
components/

```
:::
:::

#### Goal

```text
main/
├── App/
├── assets/      ← updated
├── auth/
├── layout/
└── temp/

components/      ← not copied

```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Understanding the Difference

| Action | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `git merge ui` | Merges every change from ui |
| `git restore --source=ui` | Copies selected files only |
| `git checkout ui -- file` | Copies selected files (older syntax) |
| `git restore --patch` | Lets you choose individual changes |</md></sn><sn><md>## Git Branch Sync Guide {.text-center}

#### Step 1

::: .text-center
`Check Your Current Branch`
Always confirm where you are before making changes.
:::

```
git branch --show-current
```

**Example:**
```
main
```

**Or:**
```
git status
```

**Output:**
```
On branch main
```

**If you're on the wrong branch:**
```
git checkout main
```
or 

```
git switch main
```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Step 2: 

::: .text-center
`Check Repository Status`
Make sure there are no uncommitted changes.
:::

```
git status
```

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-md-6
**Clean repository:**
```
nothing to commit, working tree clean
```
:::

:::.col-12 .col-md-6
**If you see modified files:**
```
modified: assets/style.css
```

**Either commit them:**
```
git add .
git commit -m "Save current work"
```

**Or stash them:**
```
git stash
```
:::
:::

</md></sn><sn><md>#### Step 3: 

::: .text-center
`Verify Available Branches`
List all branches.
:::

```
git branch
```

**Example:**
```
* main
  ui
```

**To see remote branches too:**
```
git branch -a
```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Step 4: 

:::.text-center
`Compare Branch Differences`
Before copying anything, inspect what actually changed.
:::

**File-level changes**
```
git diff --name-status main...ui
```

**Example:**
```
M assets/css/style.css
M assets/js/app.js
A assets/new.css
A components/navbar.php
D assets/old.png
```

+++ **Meaning:**

| Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| M | Modified |
| A | Added |
| D | Deleted |
| R | Renamed |

+++


**Compare only one folder**
```
git diff --name-status main...ui -- assets/
```

**Example:**
```
M assets/css/style.css
M assets/js/app.js
A assets/new.css
```

**See actual code changes**
```
git diff main...ui -- assets/
```

Git displays line-by-line differences.

</md></sn><sn><md>#### Step 5: 

`Understand What Can Happen` {.text-center}

**Suppose:**

```
main
assets/
    style.css
    app.js
    old.png

ui
assets/
    style.css
    app.js
    new.css
```

**Possible events:**

| Event | What happens |
|-------|--------------|
| File modified | Can be copied |
| File added | Optional |
| File deleted | Optional |
| File renamed | Review carefully |
| Same file edited differently | May cause conflict |
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Step 6: 

`Choose Your Merge Strategy` {.text-center}


:::.p-2 .border .bg-teal
**Strategy A — Copy One File**

Safest option.

```
git restore --source=ui -- assets/css/style.css
```

Now only that file changes.

**Verify:**
```
git diff
```

**Commit:**
```
git add assets/css/style.css
git commit -m "Sync style.css from ui"
```
:::



::: .p-2 .my-2 .border .bg-pink
**Strategy B — Copy Multiple Files**

```
git restore --source=ui -- \
assets/css/style.css \
assets/js/app.js
```

Only those files are updated.
:::




::: .p-2 .border .bg-orange
**Strategy C — Interactive Merge (Recommended)**

Best when both branches edited the same file.

```
git restore --source=ui --patch assets/
```

Git asks:
```
Apply this hunk? [y,n,q,a,d,s,e,?]
```

+++ **Options:**

| Key | Meaning |
|-----|---------|
| y | Apply |
| n | Skip |
| s | Split into smaller pieces |
| e | Edit manually |
| q | Quit |

+++

This gives maximum control.
:::
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Step 7: 

:::.text-center
`Review Before Committing`
Always inspect changes.
:::

**Status**
```
git status
```

**Example:**
```
modified: assets/css/style.css
modified: assets/js/app.js
```

**Review changes**
```
git diff
```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Step 8: 

`Commit Selected Changes` {.text-center}

```
git add assets
git commit -m "Selectively sync assets from ui"
```</md></sn>